From f312cb1e306b2f02777130cbd90fe570b9db8808 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sean Du <do4suki@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 4 Aug 2026 04:18:57 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] mm: mglru: update to v15 patchset

Refresh the existing MGLRU implementation through the upstream v15
14-patch series.

Adapt v14 page-table walking, reclaim control, page-flag accounting,
and userspace interfaces to the 4.19 baseline. The v14 shrink_node
refactor is represented by equivalent proportional reclaim behavior in
shrink_node_memcg(), whose surrounding reclaim flow differs from newer
kernels.

Integrate v15 aging and scan-abort heuristics in place of the old
cross-memcg swap avoidance controls, curtailing excess direct-reclaim
swapping while retaining bounded, fair reclaim work.

Use the 4.19-safe generation value when deleting LRU pages, since its
set_mask_bits() returns the new flags while the v15 code expects the old
flags. Also keep MGLRU compatibility accounting out of legacy memcg LRU
sizes.

Change-Id: Ia905af3f81e7008d2774eacc5c300d71e55324ef
Signed-off-by: Sean Du <do4suki@gmail.com>
Signed-off-by: fadlyas07 <mhmmdfdlyas@proton.me>

Conflicts:
	include/linux/mmzone.h
	mm/vmscan.c
